  "question": "I need to manage a coding project called \"Ableton Analysis\" where we analyze logs from the Ableton software. Can you help me set up a project structure to organize the tasks for analyzing logs, and then connect these tasks with specific topics of knowledge, such as \"Log Analysis Techniques\" and \"Error Management Strategies\"? Additionally, make sure tasks are systematically linked within a knowledge graph for efficient tracking and analysis.",
  "answer": "Everything is set up and verified. Here's what I built:\n\n## 📁 Project: Ableton Analysis\n**ID:** `8df87ae3-b8d6-408f-8c1b-c3b32a7506df`\n\n### Task Structure (6 tasks, 52 estimated hours)\n\n| Task | Priority | Est. | Depends On |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Collect and Ingest Ableton Log Files | 9/10 | 6h | — (entry point) |\n| Build Log Parser and Normalizer | 9/10 | 10h | Ingest |\n| Detect Patterns and Anomalies in Logs | 7/10 | 12h | Parser |\n| Classify Errors and Define Error Taxonomy | 8/10 | 9h | Parser |\n| Build Analysis Report and Dashboard | 6/10 | 8h | Pattern Detection + Error Classification |\n| Add Automated Tests and Regression Fixtures | 5/10 | 7h | Parser + Error Classification |\n\nThe dependency chain forms a clean pipeline: **ingest → parse → (pattern detection ∥ error classification) → report**, with testing layered on top of the parser and taxonomy.\n\n### 🕸️ Knowledge Graph (10 entities, 25 relations)\n\n**Knowledge topics** — each populated with concrete observations:\n- **Log Analysis Techniques** — parsing/normalization, template frequency analysis, session diffing, timeline correlation, anomaly detection\n- **Error Management Strategies** — error taxonomy, severity assignment, remediation guidance, regression prevention\n\n**Supporting entities:** the `Ableton Analysis` project node and an `Ableton Log Files` data source node (with platform paths and format notes).\n\n**Relation types used:**\n- `includes task` — project → each of the 6 tasks\n- `depends on` — mirrors the task dependency chain inside the graph\n- `applies knowledge topic` — links each task to the topic(s) it draws on (e.g., parser → Log Analysis Techniques; taxonomy → Error Management Strategies)\n- `collects` / `parses` — tasks → the log data source\n- `builds on` — Error Management Strategies → Log Analysis Techniques\n\nThis means you can now query the graph by topic to see every task that depends on it, or traverse from any task to its prerequisites and the knowledge it requires. A natural next step would be to start on **Collect and Ingest Ableton Log Files**, since it's the only unblocked task in the pipeline.",
